(7456474, 1179216, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>*scratching head* I don''t really get what Jake is on about, honestly I do not see the warped distortion - and it''s shot with a fisheye which is the epitome of warped distortion!<br/> <br/>Great exposure and tones, looks like a lot of thought went into where you were going to shoot, when and how...and I think it worked beautifully.  Nice and crisp, lots of detail.  Perhaps b/w might have come across in a more powerful fashion.  I would attribute the low score less to the actual image and perhaps more to the challenge suggestion description - it''s probably just a little too technical to actually become a real challenge.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! *scratching head* I don''t really get what Jake is on about, honestly I do not see the warped distortion - and it''s shot with a fisheye which is the epitome of warped distortion! Great exposure and tones, looks like a lot of thought went into where you were going to shoot, when and how...and I think it worked beautifully.  Nice and crisp, lots of detail.  Perhaps b/w might have come across in a more powerful fashion.  I would attribute the low score less to the actual image and perhaps more to the challenge suggestion description - it''s probably just a little too technical to actually become a real challenge. Hope this helps Susan', '2016-05-24 20:19:03.000000', NULL, 0);
